{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/714486-corporate-merger","id":714486,"title":"Corporate Merger","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-22T07:41:05-07:00","id":714486,"title":"Corporate Merger","content":"So, plot idea. What would happen if The Cheiron Group, Deva Corporation, and Last Dynasty International all were in talks for a corporate merger.<br /> <br /> Discuss?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T08:22:06-07:00","id":714606,"title":"","content":"I feel like &quot;war&quot; would not be severe enough to describe that conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T08:59:50-07:00","id":714653,"title":"","content":"Supernaturals 'in the know,' would probably breathe a sigh of relief, thinking that this would mean Mummies and Demons would become more high priority targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T09:13:47-07:00","id":714680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/714486-corporate-merger?p=714653#post714653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Supernaturals 'in the know,' would probably breathe a sigh of relief, thinking that this would mean Mummies and Demons would become more high priority targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless they happen to be Mummies or Demons.<br /> <br /> Of course, then the &quot;acquisitions&quot; teams sent after your parts now might be Sekhem-empower, Amkhat-directing, and Gadget-wielding (and with enough financial backing to economically dominate many countries) probably doesn't help you much either.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T10:36:27-07:00","id":714766,"title":"","content":"I think Cheiron is actually the larger corporation there, as well. Not entirely sure, but if it was a buyout, if you wanted you could take advantage of the drop in Deva and LDI's stocks to try and weasel some supernaturals into the field of the enemy. Provided they're publicly traded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T11:32:45-07:00","id":714837,"title":"","content":"Which is a good question. <i>Are</i> any of them publicly traded? What would they do to stop Vampire/Mage/Demon/Mummy investors from getting their claws into them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T13:15:29-07:00","id":715228,"title":"","content":"It's unclear if Cheiron is publicly traded, but they do have stocks, as there's mentions of them falling at points. So they might be privately traded. Either way it's a real interesting weak point for the conglomerate and I could see a lot of plot points revolving around that. Not just in Hunter games, either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T01:06:19-07:00","id":718047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/714486-corporate-merger?p=714837#post714837\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is a good question. <i>Are</i> any of them publicly traded? What would they do to stop Vampire/Mage/Demon/Mummy investors from getting their claws into them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Are any of those factions organized enough on a global scale to have the money to deal with global companies (which I certainly doubt in case of vampires)? And if they are, would they be willing to risk their covers since such an investment would be highly public? Of course, if they are even aware those businesses are public faces for various Hunter organizations they might be even more wary. They would not want to come under close scrutiny of those conspiracies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T01:24:17-07:00","id":718087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are any of those factions organized enough on a global scale to have the money to deal with global companies (which I certainly doubt in case of vampires)? </div> </div> </div>I don't see why not. A vampire doesn't actually need to be on the board to control a company, all they need to do is control the person who operates an investment fund.<br /> <br /> The bigger problem with both Daeva and Cheiron is that they're not normal companies. Daeva is basically a piece of infrastructure, while Cheiron seems to almost have a will of it's own. If you take over the companies, you probably end up assimiliated to the organisation (or dead if you're the supernatural being behind it).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T07:16:21-08:00","id":773085,"title":"","content":"Anyone with stock can propose just about anything. For example every few years a minority stock holder in the company I work for makes a motion to liquidate the company selling off all of the assets including real property and patents. In the U.S. All mergers are reviewed to see if the new company will become a monopoly stockholders are given a vote or offer to sell in the case of a buyout when dealing with the Hunter companies I would imagine the board of directors have enough stock to block a hostile takeover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-24T19:11:15-08:00","id":773577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madfox11</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/714486-corporate-merger?p=718047#post718047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are any of those factions organized enough on a global scale to have the money to deal with global companies (which I certainly doubt in case of vampires)? And if they are, would they be willing to risk their covers since such an investment would be highly public? Of course, if they are even aware those businesses are public faces for various Hunter organizations they might be even more wary. They would not want to come under close scrutiny of those conspiracies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vampire first edition has two rules for vampires having superhuman wealth.<br /> <br /> In one, vampire elders can have wealth equal to their blood potency trait limit times two. At 6 and above, vampires can buy global corporations like they're playing monopoly. <br /> <br /> In the second, any vampire can be the center of a web of minions, with one of the benefits being superhuman wealth, which in this case means minions with resources 4, which means the vampire is basically the lead of their own conspiracy of wealthy people. <br /> <br /> So depending on the rules used, vampires don't need an organization to do that, they can do it individually.<br /> <br /> Barring that, Danse Macabre and the forsaken chroniclers guide has rules for third tier, in the old term, vampire and werewolf organizations, mage orders are there by default.<br /> <br /> Demons and changelings can give out social merits like potato chips, and some mummies can do the same as well. Financial power, political power, criminal power, legal power, they can game the system in a way the one percenters would kill to be able to duplicate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T01:35:14-08:00","id":773735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>StSword</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/714486-corporate-merger?p=773577#post773577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire first edition has two rules for vampires having superhuman wealth.<br /> <br /> In one, vampire elders can have wealth equal to their blood potency trait limit times two. At 6 and above, vampires can buy global corporations like they're playing monopoly.<br /> <br /> In the second, any vampire can be the center of a web of minions, with one of the benefits being superhuman wealth, which in this case means minions with resources 4, which means the vampire is basically the lead of their own conspiracy of wealthy people.<br /> <br /> So depending on the rules used, vampires don't need an organization to do that, they can do it individually.<br /> <br /> Barring that, Danse Macabre and the forsaken chroniclers guide has rules for third tier, in the old term, vampire and werewolf organizations, mage orders are there by default.<br /> <br /> Demons and changelings can give out social merits like potato chips, and some mummies can do the same as well. Financial power, political power, criminal power, legal power, they can game the system in a way the one percenters would kill to be able to duplicate.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if it was that easy, the supernaturals would rule the world and the mortals would be nothing but pawns... For me it is certainly theoretically possible, but it just clashes too much with my suspension of disbelief or the types of games I prefer to run. There is a reason I prefer nWoD and the lack of global conspiracies is certainly one of them. Besides, it is a fact that people with the amount of money to buy up companies like Shell tend to draw a lot of attention, and none of the supernaturals fare well with such attention.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4560-madfox11","name":"Madfox11","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"172"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T02:17:27-08:00","id":773756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if it was that easy, the supernaturals would rule the world and the mortals would be nothing but pawns... </div> </div> </div>Not really. It means, they can own and control the top-levels of corporations. There's a big gap between the board at the top of a corporation and the bottom. At best, they control the general direction of the company.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For me it is certainly theoretically possible, but it just clashes too much with my suspension of disbelief or the types of games I prefer to run. There is a reason I prefer nWoD and the lack of global conspiracies is certainly one of them. </div> </div> </div>This is different to a global conspiracy in the Camarilla/Technocracy sense. Those were involved in covering up a huge amount of stuff whilst also enforcing a degree of control over local supernatural beings; they're about enforcing a huge amount of control. In contrast, a vampire buying a corporation is only conspiratorial in the sense that the vamprie has something to hide personally. Otherwise, it's completely mundane.<br /> <br /> Remember also, that supernatural beings really don't need to own stuff legally to control it; so buying out a corporation won't stop other supernatural beings taking over local areas of the corporation. If a vampire buys out Shell, that won't stop a Silver Ladder mage in Africa using their local Shell office's HR department as a Cryptopoly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T03:59:31-08:00","id":773804,"title":"","content":"You can be rich and still be unable to control the world. Controlling the world takes a lot of manpower, and is really unnecessary. And if you're rich enough, you don't care what Joe the Plumber is doing, you just know you can pluck him from his life if you wanted to and no one would be able to do anything, something even street level vampires can manage. Keeping in mind these are vampires they don't need to buy up companies, they can just control the owner. I'd be willing to bet most rich old people would be willing to jump for the chance to gain the limited immortality offered by ghouling.<br /> <br /> There's also the Prima Invicta from the Danse Macabre, a covenant that acts as essentially the old world vampire Illuminati, but not quite the Camarilla. They want to have access to the money and the authority because they want to have 'ultimate permission,' their own private Masquerade reinforced by the herd itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-01T15:02:17-08:00","id":777928,"title":"","content":"As to whether Cheiron Group is publicly traded, often lost in the fluff is that Cheiron is not actually a single corporation but rather a holding company for its various subsidiary ventures. Keystone Pharmaceuticals is the actual corporation that serves as Cheiron's main &quot;face&quot; in terms of consumer interaction and medical research.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-06T22:18:50-08:00","id":781561,"title":"","content":"Pentex, except functional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T23:52:16-07:00","id":860150,"title":"","content":"They talk about Cheiron group trying to buy out part of deva Corp. In mortal remains.<br /> &quot;Much to the Cheiron Group\u2019s surprise, Luminous Labs, a pharmaceutical corporation with research centers throughout the developed world, is already working on the \u201cdemon problem,\u201d from lesser demons all the way on up. Naturally, Cheiron tried to buy Luminous, only to find that it was a wholly owned subsidiary of the much larger Deva Corporation. Deva had deep enough pockets to laugh at Cheiron\u2019s offer.&quot;<br /> So I'm inclined to think Deva is the larger one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-06T08:04:57-07:00","id":860306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/714486-corporate-merger?p=860150#post860150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They talk about Cheiron group trying to buy out part of deva Corp. In mortal remains.<br /> &quot;Much to the Cheiron Group\u2019s surprise, Luminous Labs, a pharmaceutical corporation with research centers throughout the developed world, is already working on the \u201cdemon problem,\u201d from lesser demons all the way on up. Naturally, Cheiron tried to buy Luminous, only to find that it was a wholly owned subsidiary of the much larger Deva Corporation. Deva had deep enough pockets to laugh at Cheiron\u2019s offer.&quot;<br /> So I'm inclined to think Deva is the larger one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not necessarily. Luminous is fairly core to Deva's focus, while only of marginal interest to Cheiron. Luminous (through Deva) doesn't need the money, and Cheiron likely sees no value in offering more for a smaller corporation. I don't think it is the case on one being &quot;bigger&quot; but rather, Cheiron thinking Luminous was a little fish to snap up and being wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T09:43:13-07:00","id":861104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/714486-corporate-merger?p=860306#post860306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not necessarily. Luminous is fairly core to Deva's focus, while only of marginal interest to Cheiron. Luminous (through Deva) doesn't need the money, and Cheiron likely sees no value in offering more for a smaller corporation. I don't think it is the case on one being &quot;bigger&quot; but rather, Cheiron thinking Luminous was a little fish to snap up and being wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Deva's pockets don't need to be deeper than Cheiron's, just deep enough that Cheiron's bid wasn't the buy out they thought it would be. Cheiron's investigation of Luminous (and likely industrial espionage) led them to believe Luminous was a private researcher that stumbled on the Demon phenomena. Such an asset would fit neatly into Cherion's conglomerated stable so they figured they'd poach it before Luminous got too far down the rabbit hole. What they discovered instead was another shadowy corporate entity that was &quot;in the know.&quot; While this does mean Cheiron is starting at a disadvantage vis a vis Deva in terms of Demonic research and will likely have to do most of the work in-house, they've instead gained knowledge of another player on the field they were previously ignorant of. A fair trade in the grand scheme.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T10:06:32-07:00","id":861120,"title":"","content":"Honestly it seems like Last Dynasty and Cheiron Group are the two that might conceivably go in for a merger, as they have at least somewhat similar wheelhouses and agendas. Deva doesn't really have any reason to have anything to do with the other two, nor they with it. That being said, I don't think that the two would ever come to an agreement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T11:55:53-07:00","id":861186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/714486-corporate-merger?p=861120#post861120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly it seems like Last Dynasty and Cheiron Group are the two that might conceivably go in for a merger, as they have at least somewhat similar wheelhouses and agendas. Deva doesn't really have any reason to have anything to do with the other two, nor they with it. That being said, I don't think that the two would ever come to an agreement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, of course.<br /> <br /> The point of this thread was more of the &quot;Oh, shit&quot; reaction from monsters at the prospect of 3 big Conspiracies joining capital and information. I get the feeling that Deva has far better trained Operatives, and LDI gives theirs more support, than TCG's Field Projects Division (I mean, the &quot;Operations Manual&quot; is an in-universe joke).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T14:14:32-07:00","id":861288,"title":"","content":"That's always been something I love about Cheiron Group.<br /> <br /> &quot;We're a highly trained cell of covert corporate operatives! We had a retreat weekend and everything! There was a leadership seminar, trust exercises, and then they cut us open to put monster parts inside of us!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-07T14:21:17-07:00","id":861295,"title":"","content":"Hey, at least the implants are rigorously tested*.<br /> <br /> (* = They've had at least one survivable test case before. Probably. Unless the paperwork was forged.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}